<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Native support for A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2).

    That mod decides which animals may receive which prosthetics with three abstract recipes that only
    carry a recipeUsers list: ADS_Cat1 (basic replacements), ADS_Cat2 (simple prosthetics) and ADS_Cat3
    (bionics). The lists are cumulative: an animal of category 3 is in all three, one of category 2 in
    categories 2 and 1, one of category 1 in category 1 only. This is the convention its own ModCompat
    patches follow, and the one it asks other mods to follow.

    The species are placed by what they are and by how they can be trained, the same way its lists place
    vanilla animals:
      category 1  the ebbb and the bebbbholder, the two smallest (body size 0.2), critters
      category 2  the crebbb, the ebbberration, the drebbbd and the goliebbb, trainable to Intermediate
      category 3  the beee, the ebbbomination and the thrumebbb, trainable to Advanced

    Two things make this work, and both are needed.

    The guard. The operation runs only when ADS_Cat1 exists, that is when the mod is loaded. A
    PatchOperationConditional with no nomatch succeeds without doing anything when it is not. The
    MayRequire attribute cannot be used here: nothing reads it on an operation, only on a def node or a
    field element.

    The load order. ADS 2 copies these three lists into its real surgery recipes in its own last patch,
    z_Category_Patches.xml, and it copies them as they are at that moment. A name added afterwards lands in
    a list nobody reads. Patches run in mod-list order, so About.xml declares loadBefore for it.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>Ebbb</li>
            <li>Bebbbholder</li>
            <li>Crebbb</li>
            <li>Ebbberration</li>
            <li>Drebbbd</li>
            <li>Goliebbb</li>
            <li>Beee</li>
            <li>Ebbbomination</li>
            <li>Thrumebbb</li>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat2"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>Crebbb</li>
            <li>Ebbberration</li>
            <li>Drebbbd</li>
            <li>Goliebbb</li>
            <li>Beee</li>
            <li>Ebbbomination</li>
            <li>Thrumebbb</li>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat3"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>Beee</li>
            <li>Ebbbomination</li>
            <li>Thrumebbb</li>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
